      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "lDrmc3ERaeMr"
      },
      "source": [
        "#Sentinel 1 SAR Seasonal Averages for the Walpole National Park Region & Surrounds\n",
        "\n",
        "---\n",
        "\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "QQFUhGIRaydH"
      },
      "source": [
        "The below notebook will create Sentinel C-band Synthetic Aperture Radar (SAR) seasonal averages for the 4 seasons of the year over 9 years of available data. S1 SAR project data available within GEE is provided from 2014 onwards.\n",
        "\n",
        "The idea is to calculate the seasonal average for each season of every year back to 2014 or the extent of data availability and then find the average of each season for the extent of the data period.\n",
        "\n",
        "Less technically, an average of the each years season averages."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "LcejBvracBen"
      },
      "source": [
        "This collection contains all of the GRD scenes. Each scene has one of 3 resolutions (10, 25 or 40 meters), 4 band combinations (corresponding to scene polarization) and 3 instrument modes. Use of the collection in a mosaic context will likely require filtering down to a homogeneous set of bands and parameters.Each scene contains either 1 or 2 out of 4 possible polarization bands, depending on the instrument's polarization settings. The possible combinations are single band VV or HH, and dual band VV+VH and HH+HV:\n",
        "\n",
        "1. VV: single co-polarization, **vertical transmit/vertical receive**\n",
        "2. HH: single co-polarization, **horizontal transmit/horizontal receive**\n",
        "3. VV + VH: dual-band cross-polarization, **vertical transmit/horizontal receive**\n",
        "4. HH + HV: dual-band cross-polarization, **horizontal transmit/vertical receive**\n"
      ]
    },
    {
